  "what_this_kills": "The hypothesis AllCoordinatesInteractionContrastRankOne(q,F) => 2D <= (m-1) delta_square is FALSE as currently operationalized, i.e. with D measured at the Top-C set that evaluate_candidate's index-order tie-break returns. The witness is exact, rational, rank-one verified at every coordinate, and uses an admissible nonnegative normalized product (corner) reference.",
  "what_this_does_NOT_kill": "The StrictTopC form of the claim. The violation is carried by exactly 1 of 20 admissible tie-breaks; the other 19 give a doubled gap of 0.6418 or less, well under the bound. The world has a fully tied Top-C, so it is not a StrictTopC witness at all. A separate search constrained to a strictly positive Top-C margin is required before the strict form can be called dead. At m=4 the best exact ratio found under StrictTopC was 0.999982 (margin 3568861/2416412825010), i.e. approaching but never exceeding 1.",
  "methodological_note": "The float optimizer drives every extremal world onto a Top-C tie, because ties let the tie-break hand the decision an arbitrarily bad selected set. Extremal-world searches against this objective should record the Top-C margin, or the search optimizes the tie-break convention rather than the geometry."
